# Trivy suppression list -- libssl1.1 backport status.
#
# Format: one CVE per line, optional comment block above.
#
# Phase 4 (v3.10.13-16) expanded this file from the original 6 entries (Phase 1)
# to 38 entries via the Ubuntu CVE JSON API audit at:
#   https://ubuntu.com/security/cves/<CVE_ID>.json (focal/openssl status)
#
# Every entry below is one of:
#   - not-affected = vulnerable code never landed in focal's libssl1.1 (1.1.1x line)
#   - released     = Canonical backported the fix into the focal-security public
#                    pool at a version <= our 1.1.1f-1ubuntu2.24 pin.
#
# Why this is necessary: Trivy reports CVE fixes against the upstream OpenSSL
# version string (e.g. "fixed in 3.0.13").  Canonical backports those fixes
# into focal's 1.1.1f-1ubuntu2.X without changing the version prefix.  Trivy
# doesn't see the backport and flags the CVE; the entries below close that
# false-positive loop with a per-CVE audit reference.
#
# Why these entries are LIMITED to libssl1.1: it's the only package in the
# runtime image where we install a manual .deb (from the focal-security pool
# for MongoDB 4.4 mongod compatibility -- see Dockerfile libssl1.1 install
# block).  Everything else flows through apt's noble pool which Trivy sees
# directly.
#
# What's NOT suppressed (real residual exposure in code scanning):
#   - 12 libssl1.1 CVEs where Canonical only released the fix via Ubuntu Pro
#     ESM (the "+esmN" suffix in the focal description -- e.g.
#     "1.1.1f-1ubuntu2.24+esm2").  ESM is paywalled; the public 1.1.1f-1ubuntu2.24
#     deb we install does NOT include the fix.  These CVEs remain visible in
#     code scanning as a genuine tracking signal -- when this image moves off
#     MongoDB 4.4 (won't happen until either an AVX-free MongoDB 5.0+ exists
#     OR the project drops Apollo Lake support), libssl1.1 leaves with it.
#   - libssl1.1 CVEs marked "needed" or "pending" in the focal/openssl tracker
#     (Canonical agrees a fix is needed but hasn't shipped one yet).
#
# When the libssl1.1 pin is eventually bumped (Dependabot or a manual version
# refresh past 1.1.1f-1ubuntu2.24), re-validate every entry against Ubuntu's
# tracker.  Remove anything no longer applicable.  The Phase 4 audit script
# lives in CHANGELOG v3.10.13-16's Verification section if you need to re-run
# it.

# ---- not-affected (vulnerable code not in focal libssl1.1) (16) ----

